' ============================================================================
' 47 The categories and constructors of the TensorLogic GSLT.
'
' Source of Figure TL12 in ../tensor-logic/gslt.md (section 2). The classes
' restate the Types and Terms of the TL module of that section, and the
' notes restate the rewrites of section 3. They add no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. Program, Score and Check are the entry categories. A Program is a bag
'      of statements.
'   2. Stmt lists the statement constructors. Italic constructors are
'      derived (sugar), and the notes name the core forms they rewrite to.
'   3. The expression categories form a chain from Expr (the loosest level)
'      to Atom (the tightest), as the precedence table of syntax 2.2 lists.
'   4. Index expressions form the chain Ix, IxTerm, IxUnary and IxAtom.
'   5. Four token categories carry the text of the source as a String.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 47-tl-gslt-categories.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 47-tl-gslt-categories
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ClassBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor $rrs_tl_term
skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor $rrs_tl_term
skinparam PackageBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam ClassAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 40
title The TensorLogic GSLT: categories and constructors

package "Entry categories" {
  class Program {
    PComp(ss : HashBag(Stmt))
  }
  class Score {
    ScExpr(e)
    ScLet(d, s)
  }
  class Check {
    CkExpr(e)
    CkLet(d, c)
    CkDecl(v, s, c)
  }
}

package "Statements" {
  class Stmt {
    SEq(l, o, e)
    SDef(l, o, v)
    SFact(h)
    SQuery(h)
    SDecl(t, s)
    SNew(ns, p)
    SLet(d, p)
    SGroup(p)
    //SRule(h, b)//
  }
  class Conjs <<sugar>> {
    //ConjOne(e)//
    //ConjMore(e, r)//
  }
  class ProjOp {
    OpSum, OpMax, OpMin, OpAvg, OpMaj
    //OpAcc//
  }
  class Lhs {
    LBare(t)
    LNum(t, ix)
    LBool(t, ix)
  }
  class LhsIx {
    XPlain(i)
    //XNorm(i)//
  }
  class Shape {
    ShNum(ds)
    ShBool(ds)
  }
  class Dim {
    DIx(i)
    {method} DSym
  }
}

package "The functional layer (sugar, inlined)" {
  class Def <<sugar>> {
    //DFun, DLam, DOp, DConst//
  }
  class Lam <<sugar>> {
    //LamOne, LamMany//
  }
  class Body <<sugar>> {
    //BExpr, BBrace//
  }
}

package "Expressions, from the loosest level to the tightest" {
  class Expr {
    EOfConj(c)
    //EOr(a, b)//
  }
  class Conj {
    COfNeg(n)
    //EAnd(a, b)//
  }
  class Neg {
    NOfCmp(c)
    //ENot(n)//
  }
  class Cmp {
    CmOfU(u)
    //ECmp(a, o, b)//
  }
  class UOp {
    UOfAdd(a)
    //EUser(a, o, b)//
  }
  class Add {
    EAdd, ESub, AOfTerm
  }
  class Term {
    EJuxt(a, b): the join
    {method} EMul, EDiv, EMod, TOfU
    //EMatMul(a, b)//
  }
  class Unary {
    ENeg, EPos, UOfP
  }
  class Power {
    EPow(b, e)
    POfPost(p)
  }
  class Post {
    EIdx(p, ss)
    PofA(a)
    //ET(p)//
  }
  class Atom {
    {method} AName, ANum, AStr, AParen
    AApp(f, as), ACall(f, as)
    AProj(o, js, e)
    ANorm(o, k, e), ANormArg(o, k, e, a)
  }
  class Arg {
    ArgE, ArgL, ArgKw, ArgKwL
  }
  class ElemList {
    LList(es)
  }
}

package "Indices" {
  class Sub {
    SubIx(i)
    {method} the twelve slice forms
  }
  class Ix {
    IxAdd, IxSub, IxOfT
  }
  class IxTerm {
    IxMul, IxDiv, IxMod, IxOfU
  }
  class IxUnary {
    IxNeg, IxOfA
  }
  class IxAtom {
    IxVar, IxVirt, IxNum, IxStr, IxPar
  }
}

package "Keywords" {
  class FnKw {
    16 core functions, such as FStep and FSig
    //FSigmoid, FSoftmax, FLnorm, FConcat,//
    //FSum, FTranspose, FEinsum//
  }
  class AggKw {
    KSum, KMax, KMin, KAvg, KMaj
  }
  class NormKw {
    KSoftmax, KLnorm
  }
}

package "Tokens (carrier String)" {
  class Ident <<token>> $rrs_f1r3lang
  class Numeral <<token>> $rrs_f1r3lang
  class Text <<token>> $rrs_f1r3lang
  class OpSym <<token>> $rrs_f1r3lang
}

Program o-- "1..*" Stmt
Score --> Expr
Check --> Expr
Check --> Shape
Stmt --> Lhs
Stmt --> ProjOp
Stmt --> Expr
Stmt --> ElemList
Stmt --> Conjs
Stmt --> Def
Lhs --> LhsIx
LhsIx --> Ix
Shape --> Dim
Dim --> Ix
Def --> Lam
Def --> Body
Expr --> Conj
Conj --> Neg
Neg --> Cmp
Cmp --> UOp
UOp --> Add
Add --> Term
Term --> Unary
Unary --> Power
Power --> Post
Post --> Atom
Post --> Sub
Atom --> Arg
Atom --> FnKw
Atom --> AggKw
Atom --> NormKw
Arg --> ElemList
Sub --> Ix
Ix --> IxTerm
IxTerm --> IxUnary
IxUnary --> IxAtom

note right of Stmt
  **Installed rewrites (class I)**
  S1: OpAcc rewrites to OpSum.
  S2: SRule rewrites to SEq, after RuleFold
  joins the literals of the rule.
end note

note right of Atom
  **Native rewrites (class N)**
  S3 to S6: comparisons and logic become step.
  S7: sigmoid becomes sig. S8: XNorm becomes ANorm.
  S11 to S19: EMatMul, ET and the positional calls
  become EJuxt, EIdx, AProj and ANorm.
end note

legend bottom
**Reading**
|<$rrs_tl_term>  | a category of the GSLT, listing its constructors |
|<$rrs_f1r3lang> | a token category, lexed by F1r3lang |
| //italic// | a derived constructor (sugar), absent from the normal form |
endlegend
@enduml
